  "note": "Borough election, 21 January 1928, the first under Bangor's borough charter. Four members were returned for each ward from a single poll per ward; the new council then chose one member from each ward as alderman (Johnston-Kee, Davidson, Malcolm, Cathy and Gray). No contest; the four were returned unopposed. Thomas H. Gray was afterwards chosen alderman for the ward. Returned unopposed."
